1784. Check if Binary String Has at Most One Segment of Ones
LeetCode Link:https://leetcode.com/problems/check-if-binary-string-has-at-most-one-segment-of-ones/description/?envType=daily-question&envId=2026-03-06
Intuition: 
The string should contain only one continuous segment of '1's.
Once a '0' appears, no more '1' should appear after that.
If we ever see '1' again after a '0', it means there are multiple segments of '1', so we return false.

Approach :

Traverse the string from left to right.

Use a boolean variable zero to remember if we have already seen a '0'.

If the current character is '0', set zero = true.

If the current character is '1' and zero is already true, it means a new segment of '1' started → return false.

Continue scanning the string.

If the loop finishes without finding such a case, return true.


class Solution {
    public boolean checkOnesSegment(String s) {
        int n=s.length();
        boolean zero=false;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            char ch=s.charAt(i);
            if(ch=='0')
                zero=true;
            else if(zero)return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
